Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `population_evaluation_group.evaluation_group` – main identifier of an evaluation group.  
• `population_evaluation_group.evaluation_group_description` – human‑readable label of the group.  
• `population_evaluation.state_code` – State in which the evaluation was produced.  
• `population_evaluation.evaluation_description` – description that often contains the report year(s).  
• `population_evaluation.report_year_name` – semicolon–separated list of report years; filter with LIKE '%2012%'.  
• `population_evaluation_type.evaluation_type` – e.g. AREA, VOL, EXPGROW, etc.  
• `condition.condition_status_code` – to keep track of whether a condition is accessible forest land (1), etc.  
• `condition.subplot_proportion_unadjusted` – un–expanded subplot proportion for a plot/condition.  
• `population_estimation_unit.area_used_to_calculate_all_expansion_factors` – total acres represented by an estimation unit.  
• `population.expansion_factor` – expansion factor by stratum, necessary when converting a proportion to acres.  
• Join keys – the large view `population` already relates evaluation, estimation‑unit, stratum, and plot; join `condition` on `plot_sequence_number`.  
• Filter – restrict evaluations to those whose `report_year_name` contains 2012 (`WHERE report_year_name LIKE '%2012%'`).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Example exploration & build‑up queries  
(ten progressively more complex sample queries, each capped with `LIMIT 20`)

```sql
--1) Look at all evaluation groups that mention 2012
SELECT DISTINCT evaluation_group, evaluation_group_description
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation_group`
WHERE evaluation_group_description LIKE '%2012%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2) See how 2012 appears inside the population_evaluation table
SELECT evaluation_identifier, evaluation_description, report_year_name, state_code
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation`
WHERE report_year_name LIKE '%2012%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3) Join evaluation‑group to evaluation in 2012 to show one row / evaluation
SELECT g.evaluation_group,
       g.evaluation_group_description,
       e.evaluation_description,
       e.state_code
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation_group` AS g
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation`        AS e
  ON g.evaluation_group_sequence_number = e.evaluation_group_sequence_number
WHERE e.report_year_name LIKE '%2012%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4) Look at the available evaluation types for those 2012 evaluations
SELECT DISTINCT et.evaluation_type,
       et.evaluation_sequence_number
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation_type` AS et
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation`      AS e
  ON et.evaluation_sequence_number = e.evaluation_sequence_number
WHERE e.report_year_name LIKE '%2012%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5) Inspect condition proportions for plots found in 2012 evaluations
SELECT c.plot_sequence_number,
       c.condition_status_code,
       c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted,
       c.macroplot_proportion_unadjusted
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.condition` AS c
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population` AS p
  ON p.plot_sequence_number = c.plot_sequence_number
WHERE p.report_year_name LIKE '%2012%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6) Rough acreage estimate by multiplying subplot proportion by expansion factor
SELECT
  p.evaluation_group,
  p.stratum_code,
  c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted,
  p.expansion_factor,
  (c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor) AS subplot_acres_est
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population` AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.condition`  AS c
  ON p.plot_sequence_number = c.plot_sequence_number
WHERE p.report_year_name LIKE '%2012%'
  AND c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7) Largest subplot acres per evaluation group (still sample 20)
WITH cond AS (
  SELECT
    p.evaluation_group,
    c.condition_status_code,
    c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor AS subplot_acres
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population` AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.condition`  AS c
    ON p.plot_sequence_number = c.plot_sequence_number
  WHERE p.report_year_name LIKE '%2012%'
)
SELECT evaluation_group,
       MAX(subplot_acres) AS max_subplot_acres
FROM cond
GROUP BY evaluation_group
ORDER BY max_subplot_acres DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8) Add macroplot acres for the same chosen max condition
WITH cond AS (
  SELECT
    p.evaluation_group,
    c.condition_status_code,
    c.macroplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor AS macroplot_acres,
    c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor  AS subplot_acres,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY p.evaluation_group
                       ORDER BY c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor DESC) AS rn
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population` AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.condition`  AS c
    ON p.plot_sequence_number = c.plot_sequence_number
  WHERE p.report_year_name LIKE '%2012%'
)
SELECT evaluation_group,
       condition_status_code,
       macroplot_acres,
       subplot_acres
FROM cond
WHERE rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--9) Bring in evaluation_type and evaluation_description
WITH cond AS (
  SELECT
    p.evaluation_group,
    c.condition_status_code,
    c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor  AS subplot_acres,
    c.macroplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor AS macroplot_acres,
    p.evaluation_sequence_number,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY p.evaluation_group
                       ORDER BY c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor DESC) AS rn
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population` AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.condition`  AS c
    ON p.plot_sequence_number = c.plot_sequence_number
  WHERE p.report_year_name LIKE '%2012%'
)
SELECT
  cg.evaluation_group,
  et.evaluation_type,
  cd.condition_status_code,
  e.evaluation_description,
  e.state_code,
  cd.macroplot_acres,
  cd.subplot_acres
FROM cond               AS cd
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation`      AS e
  ON cd.evaluation_sequence_number = e.evaluation_sequence_number
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation_type` AS et
  ON et.evaluation_sequence_number = e.evaluation_sequence_number
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation_group` AS cg
  ON cg.evaluation_group_sequence_number = e.evaluation_group_sequence_number
WHERE cd.rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10) Final answer query – top‑10 evaluation groups for 2012 by largest subplot acres
WITH best_condition AS (
  SELECT
    p.evaluation_group,
    FIRST_VALUE(et.evaluation_type)
      OVER (PARTITION BY p.evaluation_group ORDER BY c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor DESC) AS evaluation_type,
    FIRST_VALUE(c.condition_status_code)
      OVER (PARTITION BY p.evaluation_group ORDER BY c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor DESC) AS condition_status_code,
    FIRST_VALUE(e.evaluation_description)
      OVER (PARTITION BY p.evaluation_group ORDER BY c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor DESC) AS evaluation_description,
    FIRST_VALUE(e.state_code)
      OVER (PARTITION BY p.evaluation_group ORDER BY c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor DESC) AS state_code,
    MAX(c.macroplot_proportion_unadjusted * p.expansion_factor) AS macroplot_acres,
    MAX(c.subplot_proportion_unadjusted  * p.expansion_factor)  AS subplot_acres
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population`               AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.condition`                AS c
    ON p.plot_sequence_number = c.plot_sequence_number
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation`    AS e
    ON p.evaluation_sequence_number = e.evaluation_sequence_number
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.usfs_fia.population_evaluation_type` AS et
    ON et.evaluation_sequence_number = e.evaluation_sequence_number
  WHERE e.report_year_name LIKE '%2012%'
  GROUP BY p.evaluation_group
)
SELECT *
FROM best_condition
ORDER BY subplot_acres DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

